  "question": {
    "text": "In a set of $2 n$ observations, half of them are equal to ' $\\mathrm{a}$ ' and the remaining hall are equal to ' $-\\mathrm{a}^{\\prime}$ '. If the standard deviation of all the observations is 2 ; then the value of $|a|$ is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "ycvVK",
      "text": "\n2\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "aNxfd",
      "text": "\n$\\sqrt{2}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "QsOkf",
      "text": "\n4\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "vTPRt",
      "text": "\n$2 \\sqrt{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Clearly mean $\\mathrm{A}=0$\nNow, standard deviation $\\sigma=\\sqrt{\\frac{\\Sigma(x-\\mathrm{A})^2}{2 n}}$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2=& \\sqrt{\\frac{(a-0)^2+(a-0)^2+\\ldots \\ldots+(0-a)^2+\\ldots . .}{2 n}} \\\\\n&=\\sqrt{\\frac{a^2 \\cdot 2 n}{2 n}}=|a|\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nHence, $|a|=2$",
    "image": null
  },
